   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "וְלַעֲרִיפַת הָעֶגְלָה, אָמְרִי דְּבֵי רַבִּי יַנַּאי: כַּפָּרָה כְּתִיב בָּהּ, כְּקָדָשִׁים. וּלְטׇהֳרַת מְצוֹרָע, דִּכְתִיב: ״זֹאת תִּהְיֶה תּוֹרַת הַמְּצוֹרָע בְּיוֹם טׇהֳרָתוֹ״.",
   "en": "«And» daytime is the time «for breaking the neck of the heifer,» as the Sages of «the school of Rabbi Yannai said: Atonement is written with regard to» the heifer, teaching that it is treated «like sacred» offerings, and it has already been established that all actions relating to offerings must be performed during the day. «And for purifying the leper,» it is derived «as it is written: “This shall be the law of the leper on the day of his cleansing”» (Leviticus 14:2)."
  }
